1
00:00:27,899 --> 00:00:28,339
Bro.

2
00:00:29,179 --> 00:00:29,800
The slammer.

3
00:00:40,539 --> 00:00:41,079
Bro.

4
00:00:49,060 --> 00:00:49,520
Bro.

5
00:01:08,459 --> 00:01:09,840
Bro, it's just me.

6
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:22,780
Bro,

7
00:01:22,859 --> 00:01:25,060
just make do here for a while.

8
00:01:25,219 --> 00:01:27,859
I'll find you a better place ASAP.

9
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:34,700
Bro, what are you doing?

10
00:01:35,719 --> 00:01:36,560
Can't be seen out in the open.

11
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:45,859
Where's my radish?

12
00:01:51,739 --> 00:01:53,379
Look at you, lounging around without a care.

13
00:01:53,879 --> 00:01:55,040
Smoking like a damn chimney.

14
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:57,000
Can you give it a rest?

15
00:01:57,459 --> 00:01:58,079
You're annoying as hell.

16
00:01:59,939 --> 00:02:01,879
You've got the nerve to bitch at me?

17
00:02:02,099 --> 00:02:03,219
I haven't even started on you yet.

18
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:04,760
You never do anything useful,

19
00:02:04,819 --> 00:02:06,120
and you went and found a "big bro."

20
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,680
You can't win a single fight,

21
00:02:07,799 --> 00:02:08,979
can't make a dime,

22
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:10,319
and just get your ass beat!

23
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:11,340
That Li Laogunzi

24
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,000
is still groaning in the hospital,

25
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:17,460
unable to even pay his medical bills.

26
00:02:18,199 --> 00:02:18,960
What?

27
00:02:19,539 --> 00:02:21,340
You want to chip in for his bills?

28
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:23,539
That's an easy score right there!

29
00:02:23,879 --> 00:02:25,300
Go shake down whoever beat him!

30
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:28,740
Bleed 'em dry till they pawn their shorts to sell blood,

31
00:02:29,259 --> 00:02:31,099
or you've run these streets for nothing.

32
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:36,560
No wonder you're my real mom.

33
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:56,000
Zhou Meng.

34
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,219
Wh-What are you doing?

35
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:03,139
Your hands are all red from the cold.

36
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:04,560
I'll add some hot water.

37
00:03:07,919 --> 00:03:08,639
Do you

38
00:03:09,319 --> 00:03:10,680
think we're not close enough,

39
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:12,219
so you want to boil me alive?

40
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:14,979
Well, I was worried it wouldn't be enough.

41
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:16,800
I-I'll pour some more in.

42
00:03:18,419 --> 00:03:19,139
That's so much.

43
00:03:21,219 --> 00:03:22,039
Take a break.

44
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:23,060
I'll help you wipe it down.

45
00:03:25,879 --> 00:03:26,699
That's enough, enough, enough.

46
00:03:26,780 --> 00:03:27,199
Enough!

47
00:03:29,379 --> 00:03:30,159
Y-You go take a rest.

48
00:03:30,259 --> 00:03:30,780
I-I'll wipe it down for you.

49
00:03:30,879 --> 00:03:31,520
Come on, give it to me.

50
00:03:32,719 --> 00:03:33,900
Real men aren't afraid of a little heat.

51
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:07,659
Zhou Meng.

52
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:08,879
So, um...

53
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:11,240
that friend from the other day...

54
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:12,639
Do you know how he's doing?

55
00:04:13,039 --> 00:04:13,800
Mr. Feng?

56
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:15,939
I don't know.

57
00:04:16,980 --> 00:04:18,360
Haven't even visited him yet.

58
00:04:18,740 --> 00:04:19,759
N-No need to go.

59
00:04:19,959 --> 00:04:20,860
He's almost recovered.

60
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:24,819
Um...

61
00:04:25,259 --> 00:04:26,360
I f-forgot to ask you,

62
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:27,959
when did you two meet?

63
00:04:28,660 --> 00:04:29,699
What kind of friend is he?

64
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:33,040
What do you think?

65
00:04:36,579 --> 00:04:38,360
I... I don't think anything of it.

66
00:04:39,819 --> 00:04:40,800
M-Making friends is good.

67
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:41,899
It's good to have friends.

68
00:04:43,339 --> 00:04:43,879
Really?

69
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:49,560
Zhou Meng,

70
00:04:51,339 --> 00:04:52,399
I...

71
00:04:59,220 --> 00:04:59,740
What are you doing?

72
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:04,899
Is this big truck a place for you two

73
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:06,100
to get lovey-dovey and flirt?

74
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:08,660
Deputy Director Ma, don't spread rumors.

75
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:10,600
We're wiping down the truck.

76
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:11,600
Just doing our job.

77
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:13,959
Director Ma, is something up?

78
00:05:14,139 --> 00:05:14,519
What is it?

79
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:16,500
Did my appointment as director come through?

80
00:05:17,899 --> 00:05:19,160
Director Liu, congratulations.

81
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:20,339
An order came through alright,

82
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:21,779
but it's an arrest warrant.

83
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:23,019
The police are looking for you.

84
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:24,899
Hold on.

85
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:25,980
Don't talk nonsense.

86
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:28,019
We're asking him to come to the station

87
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:29,240
to assist with an investigation.

88
00:05:29,939 --> 00:05:30,740
Comrade Liu Haizhu,

89
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,019
please come back with us

90
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:32,839
to assist with the investigation.

91
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:34,860
Comrade Officer, what did he do?

92
00:05:35,139 --> 00:05:36,360
Suspected of affray.

93
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:38,100
We'll know the rest once we investigate.

94
00:05:39,459 --> 00:05:40,259
Liu Haizhu, you're at it again—

95
00:05:40,379 --> 00:05:40,699
No, no!

96
00:05:40,819 --> 00:05:41,439
I... I didn't!

97
00:05:41,459 --> 00:05:42,660
When was I ever in an affray?

98
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:43,980
Wait, this... this...

99
00:05:44,139 --> 00:05:45,000
I'm being framed!

100
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:46,379
Whether you did or not,

101
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:47,879
just clear it up at the station.

102
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:48,579
Let's go.

103
00:05:49,319 --> 00:05:50,100
Comrade Officer,

104
00:05:50,779 --> 00:05:52,000
don't wrong a good man,

105
00:05:52,259 --> 00:05:53,720
but don't let a bad guy off either!

106
00:05:54,259 --> 00:05:55,500
Take your time and investigate thoroughly.

107
00:05:58,779 --> 00:05:59,540
Director Ma!

108
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:01,160
Liu Haizhu really is innocent!

109
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:02,379
Those guys are the real crooks!

110
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:03,980
They stole the bike and hit people first!

111
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:05,620
The Comrade Officer doesn't know the whole story.

112
00:06:05,759 --> 00:06:06,819
You have to put in a good word for him!

113
00:06:06,839 --> 00:06:08,240
Make sure the nature of this is defined correctly!

114
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:09,779
Then you tell me.

115
00:06:10,199 --> 00:06:11,040
What's the situation?

116
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:15,399
A bunch of thugs beat up folks on the street,

117
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:18,000
and Liu Haizhu was standing up for justice!

118
00:06:18,399 --> 00:06:19,819
That's not what the police told me.

119
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:21,420
Whatever the case is,

120
00:06:21,620 --> 00:06:22,899
Comrade Officer will get to the bottom of it.

121
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:23,720
He was—

122
00:06:23,879 --> 00:06:24,639
No, what about you?

123
00:06:25,779 --> 00:06:26,959
A female comrade like you,

124
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:28,579
making such a big fuss

125
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,839
over a male co-worker.

126
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:31,920
Do you just think this is unfair,

127
00:06:33,579 --> 00:06:34,720
or do you have other feelings

128
00:06:35,839 --> 00:06:36,800
for this Liu Haizhu?

129
00:06:39,459 --> 00:06:40,399
Director, I...

130
00:06:42,079 --> 00:06:43,660
I'm looking at the facts, not the person.

131
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:46,379
I just don't want a good man to be wronged!

132
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:50,620
Zhou Meng,

133
00:06:51,879 --> 00:06:53,579
let me make things clear to you today.

134
00:06:56,279 --> 00:06:57,920
I've been courting you for so long.

135
00:06:59,199 --> 00:07:00,560
You know that full well, right?

136
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:03,899
Wait, Director,

137
00:07:04,439 --> 00:07:06,160
is there any point bringing this up now?

138
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:07,439
Those are two totally different things!

139
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:08,759
It's the exact same thing!

140
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:10,839
This Liu Haizhu

141
00:07:11,319 --> 00:07:12,079
screwed up big time.

142
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:13,660
If I went and helped him,

143
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:14,819
how foolish would that make me?

144
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:17,579
He's got a wild temper.

145
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:19,120
He's aggressive and violent.

146
00:07:19,459 --> 00:07:20,879
If he dares to beat up thieves today,

147
00:07:21,060 --> 00:07:22,339
he'll dare to beat me up tomorrow!

148
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:24,899
Besides,

149
00:07:27,079 --> 00:07:27,800
he and I...

150
00:07:28,339 --> 00:07:29,920
We're practically love rivals right now!

151
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:34,660
Director,

152
00:07:35,759 --> 00:07:37,459
you should stick to the facts!

153
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:38,779
It hasn't even happened,

154
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:40,040
yet you're already making things up about him.

155
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:40,939
Does that make any sense?

156
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:43,100
Listen to you running your mouth.

157
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:49,079
So charming.

158
00:07:50,379 --> 00:07:51,720
How this incident is defined,

159
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:53,279
what you say doesn't matter.

160
00:07:53,620 --> 00:07:55,420
It all depends on what I say.

161
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,639
If I call it affray,

162
00:07:57,759 --> 00:07:58,839
then affray it is.

163
00:07:59,139 --> 00:08:00,459
If I say he was standing up for justice,

164
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:01,860
then he was standing up for justice.

165
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:03,699
Zhou Meng,

166
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:06,300
a young woman like you,

167
00:08:07,060 --> 00:08:07,920
you're educated,

168
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:09,420
and pretty to boot.

169
00:08:10,439 --> 00:08:11,360
He's just a mechanic.

170
00:08:11,420 --> 00:08:12,319
What can he give you?

171
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:15,160
You need to be with someone who has a future

172
00:08:15,279 --> 00:08:16,899
so you can have a future yourself.

173
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:18,800
"You are the company you keep."

174
00:08:18,959 --> 00:08:20,079
Who do you think that's for?

175
00:08:21,899 --> 00:08:22,660
Director Ma,

176
00:08:23,819 --> 00:08:25,399
I earn my keep with my skills.

177
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,300
I just focus on driving my truck.

178
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:31,060
I've never expected anyone to hand me a future.

179
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:33,620
Well, you've met me now, haven't you?

180
00:08:34,460 --> 00:08:35,639
You can count on me.

181
00:08:35,799 --> 00:08:36,320
No, wait...

182
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:37,320
What are you doing?

183
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:41,059
Come on.

184
00:08:42,820 --> 00:08:44,440
Whether Liu Haizhu is cleared or condemned

185
00:08:45,460 --> 00:08:46,860
hangs entirely on a word from me.

186
00:08:47,519 --> 00:08:48,860
But whether I say it,

187
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:49,779
how I say it,

188
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:51,059
and how far I go...

189
00:08:52,259 --> 00:08:53,159
doesn't that depend

190
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:55,860
on knowing who's on my side?

191
00:08:58,620 --> 00:08:59,279
Ma Limin,

192
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,480
as the head of a factory,

193
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,200
what... what kind of behavior is this?

194
00:09:03,259 --> 00:09:04,320
You'd better think it through.

195
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:07,440
The stepping stone is right under your feet.

196
00:09:07,940 --> 00:09:09,179
Do you want to get ahead?

197
00:09:09,379 --> 00:09:10,340
Do you want to climb up?

198
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:12,960
You'd better think that through, too.

199
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:25,139
Try to mediate if possible.

200
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:26,539
Keep your temper in check.

201
00:09:26,679 --> 00:09:27,399
Tell it like it is.

202
00:09:29,299 --> 00:09:29,940
Get up.

203
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:36,480
We meet again, huh?

204
00:09:37,039 --> 00:09:37,720
Comrade Officer.

205
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:39,379
He's the one who called the police?

206
00:09:40,179 --> 00:09:41,179
You called the police?

207
00:09:42,779 --> 00:09:43,200
What about it?

208
00:09:43,220 --> 00:09:44,139
Can't I call the police?

209
00:09:44,279 --> 00:09:45,700
My brother got beaten half to death!

210
00:09:46,019 --> 00:09:47,440
You think the law can't touch you?

211
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:51,179
Where do you get the nerve to call the police?

212
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:53,360
Are you really that thick-skinned?

213
00:09:53,759 --> 00:09:54,879
Didn't you guys throw the first punch?

214
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:55,340
Comrade Officer.

215
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:56,440
Did he tell you it was five of them against one?

216
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:56,980
Really?

217
00:09:57,059 --> 00:09:58,139
I know nothing about that.

218
00:09:58,299 --> 00:09:59,639
You need evidence for everything.

219
00:09:59,799 --> 00:10:01,820
Know the time and place before you bullshit.

220
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:02,460
Comrade Officer.

221
00:10:02,519 --> 00:10:03,120
They were right at our factory gate.

222
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:04,899
My brother is still in the hospital,

223
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:06,179
stuck in bed and unable to move!

224
00:10:06,179 --> 00:10:08,059
How dare you play the victim!

225
00:10:08,139 --> 00:10:09,159
Me, playing the victim?

226
00:10:09,159 --> 00:10:09,980
Let me tell you.

227
00:10:10,159 --> 00:10:11,039
This is the police station.

228
00:10:11,179 --> 00:10:12,320
This is the government!

229
00:10:12,379 --> 00:10:13,480
Here's the medical report!

230
00:10:13,620 --> 00:10:15,139
Here's the long list of your crimes!

231
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:16,279
Countless and inexcusable!

232
00:10:16,340 --> 00:10:17,059
Calm down.

233
00:10:17,299 --> 00:10:18,039
Calm down, look at yourself.

234
00:10:18,299 --> 00:10:18,919
Calm down.

235
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:19,919
Control yourself.

236
00:10:22,179 --> 00:10:22,720
All right.

237
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:24,460
I'll give you one chance.

238
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:25,679
Explain it clearly to Comrade Officer right now!

239
00:10:25,740 --> 00:10:26,039
Hurry up!

240
00:10:26,100 --> 00:10:27,340
Who the hell are you to lecture me?

241
00:10:28,659 --> 00:10:30,539
Look at this criminal's arrogance!

242
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:31,259
What are you doing?

243
00:10:31,279 --> 00:10:32,500
This criminal is completely out of line!

244
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:33,659
Control your temper!

245
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:34,440
People like him,

246
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:36,700
he's hiding among the masses

247
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:37,460
as a bad element!

248
00:10:37,539 --> 00:10:38,779
You... you didn't even see him!

249
00:10:38,899 --> 00:10:39,440
Let me tell you.

250
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:41,059
If everyone in society were like him,

251
00:10:41,220 --> 00:10:41,960
how could our country ever prosper?

252
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:42,299
That's enough from you!

253
00:10:42,299 --> 00:10:43,240
How could the people live in peace?

254
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,159
How could we achieve the Four Modernizations?

255
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:44,759
I'm telling you!

256
00:10:44,759 --> 00:10:46,139
This is a society of law!

257
00:10:46,139 --> 00:10:47,360
I'm asking you, will you speak?

258
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:48,500
Will you or not?

259
00:10:48,759 --> 00:10:49,779
Will you?

260
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:50,659
Spit it out!

261
00:10:50,700 --> 00:10:51,220
Come on!

262
00:10:51,259 --> 00:10:52,320
Say it to my face!

263
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:54,759
You'll never see the light of day!

264
00:10:55,059 --> 00:10:55,679
I think—

265
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:57,500
Get down!

266
00:11:01,379 --> 00:11:02,120
Stay still!

267
00:11:05,379 --> 00:11:06,639
Come over and protect me!

268
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:12,940
Why did you drag me here?

269
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:14,019
What did I do wrong?

270
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:15,039
Behave!

271
00:11:18,519 --> 00:11:19,860
The hostility here is suffocating.

272
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:22,059
I shouldn't stay here long.

273
00:11:25,860 --> 00:11:26,980
Reporting, Comrade Officer!

274
00:11:28,399 --> 00:11:29,519
Still squatting around here?

275
00:11:29,700 --> 00:11:30,299
Look at him!

276
00:11:30,340 --> 00:11:32,039
He was just about to beat me up!

277
00:11:32,039 --> 00:11:32,740
It was terrifying!

278
00:11:33,100 --> 00:11:33,700
I saw it.

279
00:11:33,779 --> 00:11:35,080
He didn't touch a hair on your head.

280
00:11:35,580 --> 00:11:36,460
All right, you're dismissed.

281
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:38,200
If you remember anything else, add it later.

282
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:46,879
Hey, Comrade Officer.

283
00:11:47,019 --> 00:11:47,960
Mind if I ask you something?

284
00:11:48,679 --> 00:11:50,299
About that Liu Haizhu you just brought in...

285
00:11:50,519 --> 00:11:51,200
How long will he be locked up?

286
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:54,019
Why? Got something on your mind?

287
00:11:55,419 --> 00:11:56,940
I'm a straightforward guy.

288
00:11:57,379 --> 00:11:57,940
Generous.

289
00:11:58,559 --> 00:12:00,059
Better to make peace than enemies, right?

290
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:00,840
Look...

291
00:12:04,259 --> 00:12:05,659
If he can cough up some cash

292
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:08,100
to smooth things over with my boss,

293
00:12:08,940 --> 00:12:09,779
we won't press charges.

294
00:12:09,899 --> 00:12:10,500
We can settle this privately.

295
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,259
Could you talk to him for us?

296
00:12:14,419 --> 00:12:14,899
Sit over there.

297
00:12:16,799 --> 00:12:17,240
Sit down.

298
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,960
You think you're here to haggle?

299
00:12:21,159 --> 00:12:21,960
No, of course not.

300
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:24,019
Just a humble suggestion.

301
00:12:24,379 --> 00:12:24,799
A suggestion?

302
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:25,879
Strictly speaking,

303
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,340
this counts as a mutual brawl.

304
00:12:27,539 --> 00:12:28,419
Both sides could be locked up.

305
00:12:29,059 --> 00:12:30,460
But seeing how badly they got beat up,

306
00:12:30,879 --> 00:12:32,480
all I can do is try to mediate.

307
00:12:33,399 --> 00:12:34,659
So how much can you get him to pay?

308
00:12:36,299 --> 00:12:37,580
Can you settle it for this much?

309
00:12:37,879 --> 00:12:38,860
If you can get us this much,

310
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,299
I'll make sure to take care of you.

311
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:46,399
Where do you think you are?

312
00:12:47,019 --> 00:12:48,240
Keep it up and I'll lock you up right now!

313
00:12:50,919 --> 00:12:51,519
Still not leaving?

314
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:54,159
Alright, loud and clear.

315
00:12:54,379 --> 00:12:55,519
I'll definitely make it worth your while!

316
00:13:01,919 --> 00:13:02,519
Liu Haizhu.

317
00:13:02,980 --> 00:13:04,120
Regarding the case at West Suburb Frozen River,

318
00:13:04,419 --> 00:13:06,299
where Li Canran and several others were injured,

319
00:13:06,539 --> 00:13:08,240
we're now conducting a formal interrogation.

320
00:13:08,580 --> 00:13:09,299
Watch your attitude.

321
00:13:09,460 --> 00:13:10,240
I did nothing wrong.

322
00:13:10,759 --> 00:13:11,519
They had it coming!

323
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:12,500
They're thugs.

324
00:13:12,659 --> 00:13:13,620
They're thieves.

325
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:16,340
They're thugs and thieves!

326
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:17,580
Do you have any proof?

327
00:13:17,639 --> 00:13:18,539
Did you catch them red-handed?

328
00:13:18,679 --> 00:13:19,720
Is there a police report on file?

329
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:21,620
What do you mean there's no report?

330
00:13:21,799 --> 00:13:22,960
Back when my bicycle was stolen,

331
00:13:23,100 --> 00:13:23,980
they were the ones who took it!

332
00:13:24,139 --> 00:13:25,860
I even had to go to Lijiatun to get it back myself!

333
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,600
One thing at a time.

334
00:13:27,779 --> 00:13:29,940
Right now we're talking about you hurting people at the frozen river.

335
00:13:30,379 --> 00:13:32,100
The victims are lying in hospital beds right now,

336
00:13:32,179 --> 00:13:33,340
and their medical records are right here.

337
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:35,080
The law deals in evidence,

338
00:13:35,379 --> 00:13:36,679
not what you assume.

339
00:13:37,139 --> 00:13:39,159
They threw the first punch!

340
00:13:39,639 --> 00:13:41,299
Five of them were outside our factory gate,

341
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:42,159
ganging up on Mr. Feng!

342
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:42,820
If I hadn't stepped in,

343
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:44,340
Mr. Feng would've been beaten to death!

344
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:45,860
What I did counts as standing up for justice!

345
00:13:46,139 --> 00:13:47,240
Are you just going to ignore that?

346
00:13:47,580 --> 00:13:48,600
Did you file a report then?

347
00:13:48,860 --> 00:13:50,360
Right now, the victims are the ones who filed a report.

348
00:13:50,860 --> 00:13:52,039
As for their medical compensation,

349
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:53,379
you have to give them a proper explanation.

350
00:13:54,019 --> 00:13:54,639
Come on, now.

351
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:56,519
Honestly confess exactly what happened.

352
00:13:56,860 --> 00:13:58,100
Who else was there at the scene?

353
00:13:58,440 --> 00:13:59,940
Did anyone else fight alongside you?

354
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:00,720
Speak up!

355
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:05,000
Nobody else.

356
00:14:05,940 --> 00:14:06,940
It was just me from start to finish.

357
00:14:07,559 --> 00:14:08,379
I took them all on by myself.
